Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:24:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] gugu: writes into the ZCode App's tasks-index.sqlite are
 opt-in

The bridge wrote every ACP session into the ZCode desktop App's own
`~/.zcode/v2/tasks-index.sqlite` (upsert on session/new, title sync,
rename, soft delete, workspace delete, tombstone revival), so sessions a
client like Gugu started showed up - and were renamed / deleted - in the
user's own ZCode desktop task list. That is a write into another app's
database outside the ZCode protocol, and breaks silently when the App
changes its schema. All six writers now run only with
ZCODE_ACP_TASKS_INDEX_WRITES=1; reads (hidden ids, deleted flags, title
override, known workspaces) are unchanged. The sessions themselves stay in
the ZCode CLI's own session store (`zcode --resume <id>` still finds them).

Why: Gugu drives the agent only; the user's ZCode desktop list is not its to
edit. Product-visible: sessions started from Gugu no longer appear in the
user's ZCode desktop task list.

Upstream: none yet (an opt-out switch would be the upstream shape; draft
prepared, filing needs the owner's go-ahead).

Drop when: upstream offers an opt-out we can set from the client.
